# ENGINE-UNIVERSAL-SERVICES.47 (b) — THE CONTROL FOR THE ORPHAN ARM'S CONTEXT.
#
# `default_profile_universe_control.ebnf` (`.46`(b)) is the shape for the LOOKAHEAD arm. The ORPHAN
# arm needs its own: a rule that is PRESENT under the profile that ships (it carries no `@profiles`
# list, so it is universal) and yet cannot be derived there, because its only production references
# a rule gated to another profile.
#
#   `a` is universal; its one production is `gated`; `gated` is `@profiles: ["relaxed"]`.
#   Under `pcre2` — the `@default_profile`, the profile every parse runs under unless one is
#   requested — `a` is present and unsatisfiable: a PROFILE ORPHAN, the ERROR-class finding
#   `--lint-grammar` exists to block on.
#
# Before `.47` the lint built its profile context from the FILTERED grammar (the gated rule and its
# `@profiles` list already deleted by the load-time default filter) and never added the default to
# the universe, so this grammar read `profile_orphans=0 (error; profiles=[])` and rc 0 — the
# `>= 2` guard skipped the arm on an empty universe. After `.47` the context is the unfiltered
# grammar widened by the default, and it reads `profile_orphans=1 (error; profiles=["pcre2", "relaxed"])`
# and rc 1, naming `a` under `pcre2` with the derived fix `@profiles: ["relaxed"]`.
#
#   narrow universe  {}                -> 0 findings, rc 0   (the instrument is blind, and says "clean")
#   widened universe {pcre2, relaxed}  -> 1 finding,  rc 1   (the defect, under `pcre2`)
#
# Driven by `probe_orphan_context.sh` beside this file, which asserts the AFTER reading.
@default_profile: pcre2

@entry: true
top := trivia a trivia                            -> {kind: "t"}
     | trivia b trivia                            -> {kind: "t"}

a := gated                                        -> {kind: "a"}
b := trivia "x"                                   -> {kind: "b"}

@profiles: ["relaxed"]
gated := trivia "'"                               -> {kind: "gated"}

trivia := /[ \t\r\n]*/
